---
import {
  Abilities,
  ArmorCalculator,
  DerivedStats,
  EnchantsAndConsumables,
  Mechanics,
  Racials,
  Sources,
  StatPriority,
  TalentMatrix,
} from "../features/deepDive/index.ts";
import GuideLayout from "../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
---

<GuideLayout slug="deep-dive">
  <h2>Deep dive</h2>
  <p class="lead">The math and the details. Everything here is optional.</p>
  <details class="dd" open>
    <summary>Your numbers at this level</summary>
    <p class="small muted">Worked out from the talents you have at your level. Multipliers stack.</p>
    <DerivedStats client:load />
  </details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>What changed from Classic</summary><Mechanics /></details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>Stat priority</summary><StatPriority /></details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>Armor calculator</summary><ArmorCalculator client:visible /></details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>Talent ↔ spell table (all effects)</summary><TalentMatrix /></details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>Enchants &amp; consumables</summary><EnchantsAndConsumables /></details>
  <details class="dd">
    <summary>Professions, camping, Legacy points</summary>
    <ul class="kv">
      <li>
        <b>While leveling</b>Leatherworking and Skinning. Skin the animals you kill, then make your own leather armor,
        armor kits, and later the Wolfshead Helm and the Warbear pieces.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>At 60</b>Many tanks switch to Engineering plus Leatherworking. Engineering bombs (Sapper Charges) reportedly
        work in bear form in Forever.
      </li>
      <li><b>Always</b>Cooking, First Aid and Fishing. They don't use up a profession slot.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Camping</b>Forever lets you set up a camp with useful items. Wowhead recommends the Fish Bowl (more stats),
        First Aid Kit, Sharpening Wheel, Lodestone and Camp Tent (rested experience).
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Legacy points</b>Forever's account-wide bonuses. Spend the first 5 on Thrill of Adventure, the next 5 on Well
        Rested, then Talented, then the rest on Thrill of Adventure.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>Windshaper Skyborne racials</summary><Racials /></details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>All abilities by level</summary><Abilities /></details>
  <details class="dd"><summary>Sources</summary><Sources /></details>
</GuideLayout>
